Hardwood S/G trends: 12 species (Balakshin 2016) vs the calibrated model
  measured range S/G 1.15-3.02, n=12, quantitative 13C NMR, per 100 Ar
  model compared over the SAME S/G range, %% of the six modelled linkages
  NOTE normalisations differ; compare sign and strength, not magnitude.

                measured (12 species)     model (same S/G range)
quantity           slope       r    r2       slope direction
------------------------------------------------------------------
beta-O-4           +3.88   +0.57  0.33       +2.51 same sign
beta-beta          +0.77   +0.32  0.10       +0.07 same sign
beta-5             -0.78   -0.46  0.21       -1.62 same sign
condensation       -3.50   -0.58  0.34       -1.03 same sign

The two quantities that move with S/G in the measured set are beta-O-4
(up) and condensation (down) -- the pair the S-blocks-C5 mechanism produces.
beta-beta does not move, which is also what the model does.

